msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1475
#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1506
msgid "Suggested for this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1476
msgid "Hide suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1478
msgid ""
"Other Lynbro plugins that fit what this site uses. Nothing is installed "
"unless you click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1479
msgid "All Lynbro plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1507
msgid ""
"Picked from what this site already uses — read on this site, nothing is sent "
"anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1626
msgid "Tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1627
msgid ""
"Export this plugin&#8217;s settings as a JSON backup, or reset them to "
"defaults. 100% local — nothing leaves your site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1633
msgid "Export settings (JSON)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1635
msgid "Reset all settings to defaults?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/lynbro-core/lynbro-core.php:1639
msgid "Reset to defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:39
msgid "Videos have captions, and the captions are right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:40
msgid ""
"Open each video and read the captions along with the audio. Automatic "
"captions are usually wrong about names, prices and Danish place names — "
"which is exactly the part that matters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:45
msgid "Anything shown but not said in a video is described"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:46
msgid ""
"Listen to the video without looking at it. If something important only "
"appears on screen — a phone number, a form being filled in — it needs "
"describing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:51
msgid "The reading order matches the visual order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:52
msgid ""
"Turn off the site stylesheet, or read the page in reader mode. If the "
"sidebar arrives in the middle of an article, the source order is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:57
msgid "Text is text, not a picture of text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:58
msgid ""
"Look for banners, price lists and opening hours saved as images. They do not "
"enlarge, do not translate and cannot be read aloud."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:63
msgid "The page works at 320 pixels wide and at 400% zoom"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:64
msgid ""
"Zoom the browser to 400% on a desktop. Nothing should need to be scrolled "
"sideways to be read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:69
msgid ""
"Tooltips and dropdowns can be dismissed and stay open long enough to use"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:70
msgid ""
"Hover over a menu that opens a submenu. Escape should close it, and moving "
"the mouse onto the submenu should not make it vanish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:75
msgid "The keyboard can always get out again"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:76
msgid ""
"Tab through the whole page, including any pop-up, cookie banner or chat "
"widget. If focus goes into something it cannot leave, that page is unusable "
"without a mouse."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:81
msgid "Nothing flashes more than three times a second"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:82
msgid ""
"Check animated banners and video intros. This one is a seizure risk, not an "
"inconvenience."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:87
msgid "Any time limit can be turned off or extended"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:88
msgid ""
"Booking steps, checkout sessions and carousels that advance on their own all "
"count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:93
msgid "Headings and labels actually describe what follows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:94
msgid ""
"Read only the headings. They should work as a summary of the page on their "
"own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:99
msgid "The focused element is never hidden behind something else"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:100
msgid ""
"New in WCAG 2.2. Tab down a long page with a sticky header: the focused link "
"must not disappear underneath it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:105
msgid "Nothing can only be done by dragging"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:106
msgid ""
"New in WCAG 2.2. Sliders, sortable lists and map controls need a way that is "
"a single tap or click instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:111
msgid "Navigation is in the same place on every page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:112
msgid ""
"Compare the front page, a product page and the contact page. The menu should "
"not move or change order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:117
msgid "Help is in the same place on every page that has it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:118
msgid ""
"New in WCAG 2.2. If the phone number, chat or contact link is in the footer "
"on one page, it belongs in the footer on all of them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:123
msgid "Form errors say, in words, what is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:124
msgid ""
"Submit your contact form empty. A red border is not an error message: the "
"text has to name the field and the problem."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:129
msgid "Form errors say how to put it right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:130
msgid ""
"Type an invalid postcode. \"Invalid\" is not enough — \"A Danish postcode is "
"four digits\" is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:135
msgid "Nothing has to be typed in twice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:136
msgid ""
"New in WCAG 2.2. If a checkout asks for the delivery address and then the "
"billing address, there must be a way to copy it rather than retype it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:141
msgid "Logging in does not require solving a puzzle from memory"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:142
msgid ""
"New in WCAG 2.2. A password field must allow pasting, and a CAPTCHA that "
"asks people to recognise objects or transcribe text fails this outright."
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:244
msgid "Checked, fine"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:246
msgid "Checked, a problem"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:248
msgid "Does not apply here"
msgstr ""

#: includes/manual.php:250
msgid "Not looked at yet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/queue.php:94
msgid ""
"PHP on this server has no DOM extension, so pages cannot be parsed. Ask your "
"host to enable ext-dom."
msgstr ""

#: includes/queue.php:137
msgid "Another scan tick is still running."
msgstr ""

#: includes/queue.php:169
msgid ""
"Paused: this tick was close to the PHP memory limit. The scan continues on "
"the next tick."
msgstr ""

#: includes/queue.php:188
msgid "Stopped. Starting again picks up from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:50
msgid "The page has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:51
msgid ""
"The title is the first thing a screen reader announces and the only thing "
"that distinguishes one open tab from another. Without it people navigate by "
"guesswork."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:52
msgid ""
"Give the page a title. In WordPress that normally means the post or page "
"needs a name, or the theme is not printing wp_head()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:59
msgid "The page does not say what language it is in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:60
msgid ""
"A screen reader picks its pronunciation from the language attribute. Danish "
"text read aloud with English pronunciation is close to unusable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:61
msgid ""
"The <html> element needs a lang attribute. Themes get this from "
"language_attributes(); if yours hard-codes the tag, the fix on the Fixes "
"screen can set it for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:68
msgid "Zoom is switched off on phones"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:69
msgid ""
"user-scalable=no and a maximum-scale below 2 stop someone with low vision "
"from pinching to enlarge the text. On a phone that is the difference between "
"reading the page and leaving it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:70
msgid ""
"Remove user-scalable=no and any maximum-scale below 2 from the viewport meta "
"tag, or switch on the fix that strips them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:77
msgid "The page has no main region"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:78
msgid ""
"Screen reader users jump straight to the main content instead of listening "
"to the menu on every page. With no <main> there is nothing to jump to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:79
msgid ""
"Wrap the content area of the theme template in <main> (or add role=\"main\" "
"to the element that already holds it)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:86
msgid "There is no skip link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:87
msgid ""
"Someone using only a keyboard has to tab through the whole menu on every "
"single page before reaching the content. A skip link makes that one "
"keystroke."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:88
msgid ""
"Add a link to the main content as the first focusable element on the page, "
"or switch on the skip link fix."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:97
msgid "The page has no first-level heading"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:98
msgid ""
"The h1 is what tells a screen reader user what this page is, in one line, "
"before anything else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:99
msgid "Give the page one h1 — usually the page title in the theme template."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:106
msgid "The page has more than one first-level heading"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:107
msgid ""
"More than one h1 means the page claims to be about several things at once, "
"and the outline people navigate by stops making sense."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:108
msgid ""
"Keep one h1 and demote the others to h2. Page builders often set a section "
"title to h1 by accident."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:115
msgid "A heading level was skipped"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:116
msgid ""
"Heading levels are the table of contents a screen reader reads out. Jumping "
"from h2 to h4 suggests a missing section, and people lose their place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:117
msgid ""
"Change the heading to the next level down from the one above it. Headings "
"mark structure, not size — use CSS for size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:124
msgid "A heading is empty"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:125
msgid ""
"An empty heading is announced as a heading with nothing in it — a signpost "
"pointing at nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:126
msgid ""
"Give the heading text, or remove it. Empty headings are usually left behind "
"by a page builder used for spacing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:135
msgid "An image has no alt attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:136
msgid ""
"With no alt attribute a screen reader falls back to reading the file name "
"aloud. \"IMG underscore four seven two dot jpeg\" is what your customer "
"hears."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:137
msgid ""
"Add alt text describing what the image does on this page. If it is purely "
"decorative, alt=\"\" is correct — but the attribute must still be there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:144
msgid "The alt text says nothing useful"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:145
msgid ""
"Alt text like \"image\", \"photo\", \"billede\" or the file name carries no "
"information. It passes an automated check and tells a blind visitor nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:146
msgid ""
"Describe what the image shows or what it is for. If it adds nothing, mark it "
"decorative with alt=\"\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:153
msgid "The alt text is very long"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:154
msgid ""
"Alt text is read out in one uninterrupted breath. Past roughly 150 "
"characters people stop being able to hold it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:155
msgid ""
"Shorten the alt text to the essentials and put the detail in the page text "
"or a caption, where everyone can read it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:162
msgid "A link contains only an image with no alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:163
msgid ""
"The image is the only thing in the link, so its alt text is the link text. "
"Empty, and the link is announced as \"link\" with no destination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:164
msgid ""
"Give the image alt text that says where the link goes — not what the picture "
"looks like."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:171
msgid "An image button has no alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:172
msgid ""
"An <input type=\"image\"> is a button. Without alt text nobody using a "
"screen reader knows what pressing it does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:173
msgid "Add an alt attribute describing the action, for example alt=\"Search\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:180
msgid "An inline SVG has no accessible name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:181
msgid ""
"An SVG with no title and no label is either announced as nothing or, in some "
"browsers, as a meaningless \"graphic\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:182
msgid ""
"Add aria-hidden=\"true\" if the icon is decorative and sits next to text; "
"otherwise give it role=\"img\" and an aria-label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:189
msgid "An image map region has no alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:190
msgid ""
"Each clickable region of an image map is a link. Without alt text the whole "
"map is unusable without sight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:191
msgid "Give every <area> an alt attribute describing where it leads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:200
msgid "A link has no text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:201
msgid ""
"Screen reader users list the links on a page to navigate it. A link with no "
"text appears in that list as a blank line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:202
msgid ""
"Put text in the link, or give it an aria-label. Icon-only links need a label "
"even when the icon is obvious to sighted people."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:209
msgid "The link text does not say where it goes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:210
msgid ""
"Out of context — and a link list is exactly that — \"read more\", \"click "
"here\" and \"læs mere\" all lead nowhere in particular."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:211
msgid ""
"Name the destination in the link: \"Read more about opening hours\". Same "
"length, actually useful."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:218
msgid "The link text is a raw address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:219
msgid ""
"A screen reader reads a bare URL character by character. Nobody listens to "
"that to the end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:220
msgid ""
"Replace the address with what it leads to: \"Our price list\" instead of "
"https://…/prices-2026-final.pdf."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:232
msgid "A link opens a new window without warning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:233
msgid ""
"A new tab moves the keyboard focus somewhere else and breaks the back "
"button. Sighted people notice; screen reader users often do not. This is a "
"level AAA criterion, so it is not required for the AA conformance the "
"European Accessibility Act works to — it is here because it is cheap to fix "
"and people notice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:234
msgid ""
"Say so in the link text, or switch on the fix that appends \"(opens in a new "
"window)\" for screen readers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:245
msgid "A link leads to a document that needs its own check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:246
msgid ""
"A PDF or Office file linked from the page is part of its content, and the "
"same rules apply to it. Scanned or untagged PDFs have no headings, no "
"reading order and no text a screen reader can find."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:247
msgid ""
"Open the document and check that it has real text, headings and a title (in "
"Acrobat: Accessibility check; in Word: Check Accessibility before saving as "
"PDF). Where the information fits on a web page, put it there instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:254
msgid "A button has no accessible name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:255
msgid ""
"A button announced only as \"button\" gives no reason to press it — and it "
"is usually the one that submits the form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:256
msgid ""
"Put text in the button, or give it an aria-label. For <input "
"type=\"submit\"> use the value attribute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:263
msgid "An <a> element is used as a control but cannot be reached by keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:264
msgid ""
"Without href an anchor is not focusable. Anyone who cannot use a mouse "
"cannot reach it at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:265
msgid ""
"Use a <button> for something that acts on the page, and keep <a href> for "
"going somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:274
msgid "A form field has no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:275
msgid ""
"An unlabelled field is announced as \"edit text, blank\". This is the single "
"most common reason a contact form never gets filled in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:276
msgid ""
"Add a <label for=\"…\"> pointing at the field id, or give the field an aria-"
"label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:283
msgid "A field uses its placeholder instead of a label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:284
msgid ""
"The placeholder disappears the moment someone starts typing, so anyone who "
"is interrupted has lost the question. It is also usually too faint to read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:285
msgid ""
"Add a real label. Keep the placeholder for an example of the format, not for "
"the question itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:292
msgid "A label points at a field that does not exist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:293
msgid ""
"The label looks right on screen and is connected to nothing. Clicking it "
"does not focus the field, and screen readers do not pair them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:294
msgid "Make the label's for attribute match the id of its field exactly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:301
msgid "A field asking for personal details has no autocomplete"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:302
msgid ""
"autocomplete lets the browser fill in a name, e-mail or phone number. For "
"someone with a motor impairment that is the difference between a form they "
"can complete and one they cannot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:303
msgid ""
"Add the matching autocomplete value, for example autocomplete=\"email\", "
"\"name\" or \"tel\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:310
msgid "The same id is used more than once"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:311
msgid ""
"Labels, aria-labelledby and skip links all find their target by id. With "
"duplicates only the first one is ever found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:312
msgid ""
"Make every id on the page unique. Duplicated ids usually come from the same "
"block or widget being placed twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:321
msgid "A data table has no header cells"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:322
msgid ""
"Header cells are what let a screen reader say \"Price: 249 kroner\" instead "
"of reading a wall of loose numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:323
msgid ""
"Mark the header row with <th> cells and give each one scope=\"col\" or "
"scope=\"row\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:330
msgid "A table header cell is empty"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:331
msgid ""
"Every cell in that column will be announced with nothing in front of it, "
"which is the same as having no header at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:332
msgid ""
"Give the header cell text. If the column genuinely has no name, say what it "
"holds — \"Action\", for example."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:341
msgid "An embedded frame has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:342
msgid ""
"Frames appear in a screen reader's list of page regions. With no title the "
"entry reads \"frame\", and there is no way to tell the map from the video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:343
msgid ""
"Add a title attribute saying what is inside, for example title=\"Map of our "
"office\". The Fixes screen can do this for common embeds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:350
msgid "A video may have no captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:351
msgid ""
"Without captions the video is silent for a deaf visitor. This is also the "
"criterion the Danish authority is most likely to ask about first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:352
msgid ""
"Add a <track kind=\"captions\"> to the video, or captions in the platform "
"you host it on. Only you can confirm the captions are correct — automatic "
"ones usually are not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:359
msgid "Audio on this page needs a transcript"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:360
msgid ""
"Spoken audio with no written version excludes anyone who cannot hear it — "
"and anyone in an open-plan office."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:361
msgid ""
"Publish a transcript on the same page and link to it next to the player."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:370
msgid "An ARIA reference points at nothing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:371
msgid ""
"aria-labelledby and aria-describedby name an element by id. When that id is "
"not on the page the name is silently dropped, and the element goes back to "
"having no name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:372
msgid "Correct the id, or remove the attribute and label the element directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:379
msgid "Something hidden from screen readers can still be reached by keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:380
msgid ""
"aria-hidden=\"true\" around a link or button creates a focus stop that is "
"announced as nothing. The keyboard user simply disappears into silence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:381
msgid ""
"Either remove aria-hidden, or take the element out of the tab order as well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:388
msgid "An element has a role that does not exist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:389
msgid ""
"An unrecognised role is ignored, so the element is announced as whatever it "
"was before — usually a plain box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:390
msgid ""
"Use a role from the ARIA specification, or drop the attribute and use the "
"matching HTML element instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:397
msgid "A positive tabindex changes the keyboard order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:398
msgid ""
"tabindex=\"1\" and above pull an element to the front of the tab order for "
"the whole page. The result is a keyboard journey that jumps around the "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:399
msgid ""
"Use tabindex=\"0\" for something that should be focusable in its normal "
"place, and put the markup in the order people should meet it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:408
msgid "Content moves or blinks with no way to stop it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:409
msgid ""
"Anything that moves for more than five seconds without a pause control is a "
"barrier for people with attention or vestibular disorders — and a seizure "
"risk when it blinks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:410
msgid ""
"Remove <blink> and <marquee>. Both were removed from HTML long ago and no "
"longer belong on a live site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:417
msgid "Text set in the markup has too little contrast"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:418
msgid ""
"Below 4.5:1 the text is hard to read for anyone with reduced vision, and "
"impossible in sunlight on a phone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:419
msgid ""
"Darken the text or lighten the background until the ratio is at least 4.5:1 "
"— or 3:1 for text at 24px, or 19px bold."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:428
msgid "Text has too little contrast against its background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:429
msgid ""
"This one is measured with the colours the browser actually painted, "
"stylesheet and all. Below 4.5:1 a large share of your visitors over fifty "
"are straining to read it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/rules.php:430
msgid ""
"Adjust the colours in the theme or the block until the ratio reaches 4.5:1 — "
"3:1 for large text."
msgstr ""

